2
00:02:58,265 --> 00:03:02,198
[ Horse Whinnying ]

3
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:07,132
[ Metal Scraping ]

4
00:03:09,067 --> 00:03:11,693
[ Swishing Sound ]

5
00:03:25,471 --> 00:03:28,369
[ Panting ]

6
00:03:31,472 --> 00:03:34,529
[ Thunderclaps ]

7
00:03:38,406 --> 00:03:40,998
- [ Gasps ] - [ Thunderclaps ]

8
00:03:47,675 --> 00:03:49,971
[ Horse Snorts ]

9
00:03:52,042 --> 00:03:54,031
[ Metal Scraping ]

10
00:04:13,330 --> 00:04:16,126
- [ Alarm Bell Ringing ] - [ Man ] Help here ! Lend a hand here !

11
00:04:16,126 --> 00:04:18,186
- [ Ringing ] - Anyone .

12
00:04:18,186 --> 00:04:20,526
Constable Crane .

13
00:04:20,526 --> 00:04:23,360
Ichabod Crane ! Is that you ?

14
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:26,364
None other . Not only me .

15
00:04:26,364 --> 00:04:28,558
I have found something .

16
00:04:28,558 --> 00:04:30,792
which was lately a man .

17
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:38,361
- Burn it . - Yes , sir .

18
00:04:38,361 --> 00:04:41,060
Just a moment . We do not yet know the cause of death .

19
00:04:41,060 --> 00:04:44,034
When you find them in the river , cause of death is drowning .

20
00:04:44,034 --> 00:04:47,194
Possibly so , if there is water in the lungs . But by pathology ,

21
00:04:47,194 --> 00:04:49,202
we might be able to determine whether or not he was dead

22
00:04:49,202 --> 00:04:50,702
before he went into the river .

23
00:04:50,702 --> 00:04:52,963
I will need to examine the body .

24
00:04:52,963 --> 00:04:55,595
Cut him up . Are we heathens ?

25
00:04:55,595 --> 00:04:58,535
What happened to him ?

26
00:04:58,535 --> 00:05:00,799
Nothing , sir . Arrested for burglary .

27
00:05:05,273 --> 00:05:07,535
[ Screaming ]

28
00:05:07,535 --> 00:05:10,767
- [ Trap Door Slams Shut ] - Good work .

29
00:05:10,767 --> 00:05:13,773
[ Crane ] The millennium is almost upon us .

30
00:05:13,773 --> 00:05:16,865
In a few months. we will be living in the 19th century .

31
00:05:16,865 --> 00:05:20,965
Yet our courts continue to rely on medieval devices of torture .

32
00:05:20,965 --> 00:05:25,271
- Stand down . - I stand up for sense and justice .

33
00:05:25,271 --> 00:05:28,640
Our jails overflow with men and women convicted on confessions

34
00:05:28,640 --> 00:05:32,269
. worth no more than this one . - Constable Crane .

35
00:05:32,269 --> 00:05:35,869
This is a song we have heard from you more than once .

36
00:05:35,869 --> 00:05:40,140
Now. there are two courses open to me .

37
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:44,010
First , I can let you cool your heels in the cells ...

38
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:46,445
until you learn respect for the dignity

39
00:05:46,445 --> 00:05:48,208
. of my office . - I beg pardon .

40
00:05:48,208 --> 00:05:52,374
But why am I the only one who sees that to solve crimes ... .

41
00:05:52,374 --> 00:05:55,813
... to detect the guilty , we must use our brains

42
00:05:55,813 --> 00:05:58,349
. to recognize vital clues ...

43
00:05:58,349 --> 00:06:00,473
using up-to-date scientific techniques ?

44
00:06:00,473 --> 00:06:04,506
Which brings me to the second course .

45
00:06:04,506 --> 00:06:08,312
There is a town upstate , two days ' journey to the north ...

46
00:06:08,312 --> 00:06:10,374
in the Hudson highlands .

47
00:06:10,374 --> 00:06:14,146
It is a place called Sleepy Hollow .

48
00:06:14,146 --> 00:06:16,152
Have you heard of it ?

49
00:06:16,152 --> 00:06:18,345
I have not .

50
00:06:18,345 --> 00:06:21,511
An isolated farming community , mainly Dutch .

51
00:06:21,511 --> 00:06:26,850
Three persons have been murdered there , all within a fortnight .

52
00:06:26,850 --> 00:06:29,889
Each one found with the head ... ..

53
00:06:29,889 --> 00:06:32,615
... lopped off . - Lopped off ?

54
00:06:32,615 --> 00:06:35,622
Clean as dandelion heads , apparently .

55
00:06:37,957 --> 00:06:42,050
You will take these experimentations of yours to Sleepy Hollow ,

56
00:06:42,050 --> 00:06:45,785
and there you will detect the murderer .

57
00:06:45,785 --> 00:06:50,189
Bring him here to face our good justice .

58
00:06:50,189 --> 00:06:52,193
Will you do this ?

59
00:06:52,193 --> 00:06:53,152
I shall .

60
00:06:55,294 --> 00:06:59,022
Remember , it is you ,

61
00:06:59,022 --> 00:07:00,857
Ichabod Crane .

62
00:07:00,857 --> 00:07:05,794
who is now put to the test .

63
00:09:42,092 --> 00:09:44,422
[ Animal Howling ]

64
00:11:47,796 --> 00:11:49,853
[ Knocking ]

65
00:11:57,131 --> 00:11:58,210
[ Music ]

66
00:12:04,532 --> 00:12:07,260
[ Excited Chattering ]

67
00:12:09,100 --> 00:12:12,157
The Pickety Witch . The Pickety Witch .

68
00:12:12,157 --> 00:12:15,292
Who 's got a kiss for the Pickety Witch ? The Pickety Witch .

69
00:12:15,292 --> 00:12:19,164
The Pickety Witch . Who 's got a kiss for the Pickety Witch ?

70
00:12:20,236 --> 00:12:22,327
Is it Theodore ?

71
00:12:22,327 --> 00:12:24,733
Your pardon , miss . I am a stranger .

72
00:12:24,733 --> 00:12:27,133
Then have a kiss on account .

73
00:12:34,138 --> 00:12:37,037
I am looking for Baltus Van Tassel .

74
00:12:37,037 --> 00:12:40,128
I am his daughter , Katrina Van Tassel .

75
00:12:40,128 --> 00:12:42,728
And who are you , friend ? We have not heard your name yet .

76
00:12:42,728 --> 00:12:45,534
I have not said it . Excuse me .

77
00:12:45,534 --> 00:12:48,130
- You need some manners . - Brom .

78
00:12:48,130 --> 00:12:50,173
Come , come . We will have no raised voices .

79
00:12:50,173 --> 00:12:53,333
It is only to raise spirits during this dark time

80
00:12:53,333 --> 00:12:57,342
that I and my dear wife are giving this little party .

81
00:12:57,342 --> 00:13:01,467
Young sir , you are most welcome , even if you are selling something .

82
00:13:01,467 --> 00:13:03,476
Thank you , sir .

83
00:13:03,476 --> 00:13:06,408
I am Constable Ichabod Crane sent to you from New York

84
00:13:06,408 --> 00:13:08,636
to investigate murder in Sleepy Hollow .

85
00:13:08,636 --> 00:13:12,167
Then Sleepy Hollow is grateful to you , Constable Crane .

86
00:13:12,167 --> 00:13:15,178
And we hope you will honor us by remaining in this house .

87
00:13:15,178 --> 00:13:17,179
Well spoke , dear .

88
00:13:17,179 --> 00:13:19,906
Come sir , we will get you settled . Play on .

89
00:13:19,906 --> 00:13:24,004
[ Music Continues ]

90
00:13:26,214 --> 00:13:28,272
Excuse me , please .

91
00:13:33,549 --> 00:13:35,379
Thank you .

92
00:13:35,379 --> 00:13:38,281
Please tell Mr. Van Tassel I will be down in a moment .

93
00:13:38,281 --> 00:13:40,283
I will , sir .

94
00:13:43,251 --> 00:13:45,616
Thank God you 're here .

95
00:13:50,286 --> 00:13:53,912
[ Door Creaking ]

96
00:13:55,154 --> 00:13:58,245
Ah , excellent . Come in .

97
00:13:58,245 --> 00:14:02,253
Leave us. my dear .

98
00:14:04,822 --> 00:14:06,845
We are joined by Dr. Thomas Lancaster ,

99
00:14:06,845 --> 00:14:08,980
Reverend Steenwyck .

100
00:14:08,980 --> 00:14:11,852
our able magistrate Samuel Philipse ,

101
00:14:11,852 --> 00:14:15,549
and lastly , this fine fellow is James Hardenbrook ,

102
00:14:15,549 --> 00:14:19,058
- our notary . - And you , sir ?

103
00:14:19,058 --> 00:14:23,023
A simple farmer who has prospered .

104
00:14:23,023 --> 00:14:25,718
The town looks to me as friend and counsel .

105
00:14:25,718 --> 00:14:28,692
And landlord , and banker . Can we proceed ?

106
00:14:28,692 --> 00:14:31,090
Thank you .

107
00:14:31,090 --> 00:14:33,150
So

108
00:14:35,327 --> 00:14:38,852
three persons murdered .

109
00:14:38,852 --> 00:14:42,884
First , Peter Van Garrett ...

110
00:14:42,884 --> 00:14:46,020
and his son , Dirk Van Garrett .

111
00:14:46,020 --> 00:14:50,053
Both of them strong ,

112
00:14:50,053 --> 00:14:52,063
capable men ,

113
00:14:52,063 --> 00:14:54,689
found together ,

114
00:14:54,689 --> 00:14:56,856
decapitated .

115
00:14:59,199 --> 00:15:02,654
One week later , the Widow Winship .

116
00:15:02,654 --> 00:15:05,632
Also ... decapitated .

117
00:15:07,667 --> 00:15:12,566
Now , I will need to ask you many questions .

118
00:15:12,566 --> 00:15:14,897
But first , let me ask :

119
00:15:14,897 --> 00:15:17,026
Is anyone suspected ?

120
00:15:20,003 --> 00:15:23,868
How much have your superiors explained to you , Constable ?

121
00:15:25,504 --> 00:15:30,699
Only that the three were slain in open ground ,

122
00:15:30,699 --> 00:15:33,068
their heads found severed from their bodies .

123
00:15:33,068 --> 00:15:34,662
Hmm .

124
00:15:34,662 --> 00:15:39,105
Their heads were not found severed . Their heads were not found at all .

125
00:15:42,140 --> 00:15:46,005
- The heads are ... gone ? - Taken .

126
00:15:46,005 --> 00:15:49,474
Taken by the Headless Horseman .

127
00:15:49,474 --> 00:15:51,702
Taken back to Hell .

128
00:15:53,177 --> 00:15:55,234
Pardon . I don 't - -

129
00:15:55,234 --> 00:15:57,333
Perhaps you had better sit down .

130
00:15:58,577 --> 00:15:59,576
Yes .

131
00:16:05,745 --> 00:16:07,939
The Horseman was a Hessian mercenary ...

132
00:16:07,939 --> 00:16:10,445
sent to these shores by German princes ...

133
00:16:10,445 --> 00:16:13,570
to keep Americans under the yoke of England .

134
00:16:13,570 --> 00:16:17,944
But unlike his compatriots who came for money ,

135
00:16:17,944 --> 00:16:21,675
the Horseman came for love of carnage .

136
00:16:21,675 --> 00:16:25,442
When battle was joined , there you 'd find him .

137
00:16:27,949 --> 00:16:31,746
He rode agiant blacksteed named Dared evil .

138
00:16:31,746 --> 00:16:33,750
Aah ! Aah !

139
00:16:33,750 --> 00:16:37,841
He was infamous for riding his horse hard into battle .

140
00:16:37,841 --> 00:16:40,749
chopping off heads at full gallop .

141
00:16:40,749 --> 00:16:44,411
He had filed his teeth down to sharp points ...

142
00:16:44,411 --> 00:16:46,850
to add to the ferocity of his appearance .

143
00:16:49,153 --> 00:16:50,592
[ Snarling ]

144
00:16:53,655 --> 00:16:54,734
[ Gunshot ]

145
00:16:56,688 --> 00:17:00,451
This butcher didn 't finally reach his end until the winter of ' 79 .

146
00:17:03,256 --> 00:17:05,620
not far from here in our Western Woods .

147
00:17:05,620 --> 00:17:06,699
[ Gunshot ]

148
00:17:08,824 --> 00:17:13,417
[ Gunshots Continue ]

149
00:17:33,695 --> 00:17:36,787
- Shh . - [ Twig Snaps ]

150
00:17:58,633 --> 00:18:00,532
[ Panting ]

151
00:18:00,532 --> 00:18:03,033
They chopped off his head with his own sword .

152
00:18:03,033 --> 00:18:06,694
Even today. the Western Woods is a haunted place ... ...

153
00:18:06,694 --> 00:18:09,258
where brave men will not venture .

154
00:18:11,770 --> 00:18:14,793
For what was planted in the ground that day ...

155
00:18:14,793 --> 00:18:16,893
was a seed of evil .

156
00:18:16,893 --> 00:18:19,960
[ Whinnying ]

157
00:18:19,960 --> 00:18:22,470
And so it has been for 20 years .

158
00:18:22,470 --> 00:18:24,629
But now the Hessian wakes .

159
00:18:24,629 --> 00:18:29,229
He 's on the rampage . cutting off heads where he finds them .

160
00:18:34,307 --> 00:18:38,866
Are you saying - - Is that what you believe ?

161
00:18:40,275 --> 00:18:42,968
Seeing is believing .

162
00:18:44,442 --> 00:18:46,704
They tell me you have brought books and trappings ...

163
00:18:46,704 --> 00:18:49,572
of scientific investigation .

164
00:18:49,572 --> 00:18:53,440
This is the only book I recommend you read .

165
00:19:01,012 --> 00:19:02,944
[ Crane ] I see .

166
00:19:04,546 --> 00:19:08,411
Reverend Steenwyck . Gentlemen .

167
00:19:10,114 --> 00:19:12,945
Murder needs no ghosts to come from the grave .

168
00:19:12,945 --> 00:19:17,538
We have murder sin in New York without benefit of ghouls and goblins .

169
00:19:17,538 --> 00:19:19,980
You 're a long way from New York , Constable .

170
00:19:19,980 --> 00:19:24,073
The assassin is a man of flesh and blood ,

171
00:19:24,073 --> 00:19:27,520
and I will discover him .

172
00:19:32,356 --> 00:19:34,878
[ Owl Hooting ]

173
00:19:45,691 --> 00:19:49,249
[ Bleating ]

174
00:20:06,328 --> 00:20:08,419
Come out , devil .

175
00:20:17,664 --> 00:20:20,960
[ Hoof beats Approaching ]

176
00:20:23,531 --> 00:20:25,430
[ Gunshot ]

177
00:20:25,430 --> 00:20:28,932
[ Horse Whinnying ]

178
00:20:52,104 --> 00:20:54,037
[ Thunderclaps ]

179
00:20:54,037 --> 00:20:55,475
[ Quacking ]

180
00:21:00,505 --> 00:21:02,438
His name 's Gunpowder .

181
00:21:02,438 --> 00:21:07,530
He should do just fine , Mr. Killian , Thank you .

182
00:21:07,530 --> 00:21:09,539
Good luck , sir . If you need help , call my name .

183
00:21:09,539 --> 00:21:11,470
Much appreciated .

184
00:21:11,470 --> 00:21:14,234
Don 't you worry about a thing .

185
00:21:14,234 --> 00:21:16,968
Everything 's going to be just fine .

186
00:21:18,175 --> 00:21:21,972
Thomas ! Inside !

187
00:21:21,972 --> 00:21:24,009
Run along for your breakfast .

188
00:21:24,009 --> 00:21:26,304
Kiss your mother once for you and twice for me .

189
00:21:26,304 --> 00:21:29,708
- [ Gunshot ] - Murder . The Horseman 's killed again .

190
00:21:29,708 --> 00:21:32,801
All right , Gunpowder , we 're off .

191
00:21:32,801 --> 00:21:35,538
Come on . No , no .

192
00:21:35,538 --> 00:21:39,238
- Come on , the other way . Turn around . - Hyah .

193
00:21:43,813 --> 00:21:46,405
Good horsie .

194
00:21:55,716 --> 00:21:57,648
Mr. Miller ,

195
00:21:57,648 --> 00:22:00,706
... . ride back for the coffin cart . - Yes , sir .

196
00:22:00,706 --> 00:22:04,581
The rest of you , keep a sharp lookout .

197
00:22:04,581 --> 00:22:07,084
It 's all right . I am here now .

198
00:22:31,123 --> 00:22:34,612
The fourth victim , Jonathan Masbath .

199
00:22:37,858 --> 00:22:38,577
I see .

200
00:22:40,058 --> 00:22:43,218
And ... the head ?

201
00:22:43,218 --> 00:22:43,938
Taken .

202
00:22:45,992 --> 00:22:46,712
Taken .

203
00:22:48,026 --> 00:22:49,959
Interesting .

204
00:22:49,959 --> 00:22:51,788
- Very interesting . - What is ?

205
00:22:51,788 --> 00:22:54,918
In headless corpse cases of this sort ,

206
00:22:54,918 --> 00:22:57,654
the head is removed to prevent identification of the body .

207
00:22:57,654 --> 00:23:00,286
But we know this was Jonathan Masbath .

208
00:23:00,286 --> 00:23:03,556
Precisely . So why was the head removed ?

209
00:23:03,556 --> 00:23:06,460
- Why ? - Right .

210
00:23:07,863 --> 00:23:10,092
- You have moved the body ? - I did .

211
00:23:10,092 --> 00:23:13,255
- You must never move the body . - Why not ?

212
00:23:13,255 --> 00:23:15,263
Because .

213
00:23:29,668 --> 00:23:31,691
The stride is gigantic .

214
00:23:33,468 --> 00:23:35,730
The attacker rode Masbath down ,

215
00:23:37,136 --> 00:23:40,227
turned his horse .

216
00:23:40,227 --> 00:23:43,498
Came back . Came back to claim the head .

217
00:23:59,307 --> 00:24:01,796
[ Powder Sizzling ]

218
00:24:01,796 --> 00:24:06,603
Yes . There 's a chemical reaction .

219
00:24:06,603 --> 00:24:09,869
It shows there was a powerful , singular thrust to the neck .

220
00:24:23,111 --> 00:24:24,110
Now .

221
00:24:35,414 --> 00:24:37,778
[ Gasps ] Interesting .

222
00:24:37,778 --> 00:24:40,473
What is it ?

223
00:24:40,473 --> 00:24:44,674
The wound was cauterized in the very instant

224
00:24:44,674 --> 00:24:47,613
as though the blade itself were red-hot .

225
00:24:47,613 --> 00:24:50,615
And yet , no blistering , no scorched flesh .

226
00:24:52,517 --> 00:24:54,608
The devil 's fire .

227
00:25:01,018 --> 00:25:04,849
[ Reverend Steenwyck ] " Be vigilant . " as it sayeth in the Book of Peter .

228
00:25:04,849 --> 00:25:07,010
Chapter 5 , Verse 8 .

229
00:25:07,010 --> 00:25:09,019
" Because your adversary , the devil ,

230
00:25:09,019 --> 00:25:13,986
" as a roaring lion , walketh about .

231
00:25:13,986 --> 00:25:16,680
Seeking whom he may devour . "

232
00:25:16,680 --> 00:25:19,277
God rest . Jonathan Masbath .

233
00:25:46,827 --> 00:25:49,623
Mr. Constable , sir .

234
00:25:49,623 --> 00:25:51,854
Ah . You 're young Masbath .

235
00:25:51,854 --> 00:25:55,827
I was young Masbath , but now the only one .

236
00:25:55,827 --> 00:25:57,828
Masbath , at your service .

237
00:25:57,828 --> 00:26:01,522
In honor bound to avenge my father .

238
00:26:01,522 --> 00:26:05,120
Well , one and only Masbath , I thank you very much ,

239
00:26:05,120 --> 00:26:07,130
but your mother will need you more than I.

240
00:26:08,432 --> 00:26:10,523
My mother is in Heaven , sir .

241
00:26:10,523 --> 00:26:13,121
She has my father now to care for her .

242
00:26:13,121 --> 00:26:17,689
But you have no one to serve you . I am your man , sir .

243
00:26:17,689 --> 00:26:21,494
Yes , and a brave one too . But I cannot be the one to look after you .

244
00:26:23,335 --> 00:26:28,200
I am sorry for your loss , young Mr. Masbath .

245
00:26:39,537 --> 00:26:41,936
- Constable Crane . - Mr. Philipse .

246
00:26:41,936 --> 00:26:44,267
Something you should know .

247
00:26:44,267 --> 00:26:49,465
Jonathan Masbath was not the fourth victim , but the fifth .

248
00:26:49,465 --> 00:26:51,869
- The fifth ? - Aye .

249
00:26:51,869 --> 00:26:56,464
Five victims in four graves .

250
00:27:06,576 --> 00:27:09,474
Young Masbath .

251
00:27:09,474 --> 00:27:13,340
Find a place in the Van Tassel 's servants ' quarters . Wake me before dawn .

252
00:27:13,340 --> 00:27:16,706
I hope you have a strong stomach .

253
00:27:18,211 --> 00:27:20,178
Peter Van Garrett .

254
00:27:20,178 --> 00:27:22,734
Dirk Van Garrett .

255
00:27:22,734 --> 00:27:24,676
Jonathan Masbath .

256
00:27:24,676 --> 00:27:28,975
Five victims , four graves .

257
00:27:42,326 --> 00:27:45,781
The Widow Winship .

258
00:27:53,628 --> 00:27:56,389
[ Groans ]

259
00:28:10,631 --> 00:28:13,462
[ Crane ] Bring the widow in .

260
00:28:13,462 --> 00:28:15,623
This is most irregular , Constable .

261
00:28:15,623 --> 00:28:18,291
I should hope so , but in this case , necessary .

262
00:28:18,291 --> 00:28:20,559
We need to operate immediately .

263
00:28:20,559 --> 00:28:23,225
Operate ? She 's dead .

264
00:28:23,225 --> 00:28:28,233
When we say " operate " we mean , of course , I will need the operating table .

265
00:28:31,902 --> 00:28:35,994
Once more , the neck wound cauterized .

266
00:28:35,994 --> 00:28:41,162
The ... sword thrust to the stomach , the same .

267
00:28:41,162 --> 00:28:42,725
But to what purpose ?

268
00:28:42,725 --> 00:28:45,430
To what is your purpose , is the question .

269
00:28:46,538 --> 00:28:48,936
What manner of instruments are these ?

270
00:28:48,936 --> 00:28:52,563
Some of my own design .

271
00:28:52,563 --> 00:28:55,162
All right , then . Step outside , young Masbath .

272
00:28:55,162 --> 00:28:57,569
Thank you very much for your help . Mr. Killian .

273
00:28:57,569 --> 00:28:59,629
And if you don 't mind , Doctor .

274
00:28:59,629 --> 00:29:04,766
My concentration suffers greatly when I am observed .

275
00:29:08,009 --> 00:29:10,475
[ Indistinct Chattering ]

276
00:29:42,515 --> 00:29:44,572
I am finished .

277
00:29:44,572 --> 00:29:47,081
What , in the name of God , have you done to her ?

278
00:29:47,081 --> 00:29:49,809
We are dealing with a madman .

279
00:29:49,809 --> 00:29:51,849
What did you find out ?

280
00:29:51,849 --> 00:29:55,078
The Widow Winship was with child .

281
00:29:57,452 --> 00:29:59,281
[ Owl Hooting ]

282
00:30:12,687 --> 00:30:15,153
[ Hooves Clopping ] [ Horse Snorting ]

283
00:30:16,555 --> 00:30:20,488
[ Frogs Croaking " Ichabod " ]

284
00:30:20,488 --> 00:30:23,489
[ Croaking Continues ]

285
00:30:30,324 --> 00:30:33,757
[ Horse Whinnying ]

286
00:30:33,757 --> 00:30:34,607
[ Hooves Clopping ]

287
00:30:40,426 --> 00:30:43,415
Who 's there ?

288
00:31:12,399 --> 00:31:14,763
[ Whinnying ]

289
00:31:36,603 --> 00:31:40,162
[ Laughing ]

290
00:31:40,162 --> 00:31:43,671
[ Laughing Continues ]

291
00:31:45,739 --> 00:31:49,194
[ Woman 's Voice ] Ichabod

292
00:31:49,194 --> 00:31:50,034
Ichabod

293
00:31:53,073 --> 00:31:53,913
Ichabod

294
00:32:30,114 --> 00:32:33,808
[ Thunderclaps ]

295
00:32:49,284 --> 00:32:51,216
[ Gasps ]

296
00:33:16,286 --> 00:33:18,844
Oh . Pardon my intrusion .

297
00:33:18,844 --> 00:33:20,852
- I saw a light . - It is no intrusion .

298
00:33:20,852 --> 00:33:24,512
I come here to read when I am wakeful .

299
00:33:28,989 --> 00:33:32,649
- To read books which you must hide ? - They were my mother 's books .

300
00:33:32,649 --> 00:33:34,621
My father believes tales of romance ...

301
00:33:34,621 --> 00:33:36,622
because the brain fever that killed my mother .

302
00:33:36,622 --> 00:33:39,850
She died two years ago come mid-winter .

303
00:33:39,850 --> 00:33:43,482
The nurse who cared for her during her sickness is now Lady Van Tassel .

304
00:33:44,958 --> 00:33:47,186
There was something else too .

305
00:33:47,186 --> 00:33:49,350
Why did no one think to mention

306
00:33:49,350 --> 00:33:51,790
. that the Van Garretts are kin to the Van Tassels ?

307
00:33:51,790 --> 00:33:54,621
Because there is hardly a household in Sleepy Hollow ...

308
00:33:54,621 --> 00:33:57,353
that is not connected to every other by blood or marriage .

309
00:33:57,353 --> 00:33:59,087
I see .

310
00:34:04,629 --> 00:34:07,095
This land we 're looking at was Van Garrett land ,

311
00:34:07,095 --> 00:34:10,096
given to my father when I was in swaddling clothes .

312
00:34:10,096 --> 00:34:12,289
The Van Garretts were the richest family around these parts .

313
00:34:12,289 --> 00:34:14,455
When my father brought us to Sleepy Hollow .

314
00:34:14,455 --> 00:34:17,362
Van Garrett set him up with an acre and a broken-down cottage .

315
00:34:17,362 --> 00:34:21,660
My father worked hard for his family . and prospered and built this house .

316
00:34:21,660 --> 00:34:25,028
I owe my happiness to him .

317
00:34:25,028 --> 00:34:28,191
I remember living poor in the cottage .

318
00:34:28,191 --> 00:34:31,791
- Should I show you ? - Yes .

319
00:34:34,435 --> 00:34:38,198
Take this . It is my gift for you .

320
00:34:38,198 --> 00:34:40,667
No , I have no use for it .

321
00:34:40,667 --> 00:34:43,600
Are you so certain of everything ?

322
00:34:53,938 --> 00:34:56,496
It was your mother 's .

323
00:34:56,496 --> 00:35:00,369
Keep it close to your heart . It is sure protection against harm .

324
00:35:05,107 --> 00:35:07,266
Are you so certain of everything ?

325
00:35:22,877 --> 00:35:26,332
These are strange , these markings . What are they ?

326
00:35:26,332 --> 00:35:29,639
I have had them since I can remember .

327
00:35:39,580 --> 00:35:43,707
I used to play by this hearth as a child .

328
00:35:46,015 --> 00:35:49,641
It was my first drawing school , and my mother was my teacher .

329
00:35:51,882 --> 00:35:53,644
Look .

330
00:35:53,644 --> 00:35:56,046
See ? Carved into the fireback ?

331
00:35:56,046 --> 00:35:59,379
The Archer . I 'd forgotten it .

332
00:36:01,884 --> 00:36:04,476
This was from long before we lived here .

333
00:36:06,952 --> 00:36:10,113
- Are you all right ? - Yes , thank you .

334
00:36:10,113 --> 00:36:13,312
- [ Bird Chirping ] - A cardinal .

335
00:36:13,312 --> 00:36:15,182
My favorite .

336
00:36:15,182 --> 00:36:17,981
I 'd love to have a tame one , but I wouldn 't have the heart to cage him .

337
00:36:19,588 --> 00:36:23,112
Well , then , I ... have something for you .

338
00:36:24,756 --> 00:36:27,916
Cardinal on one side .

339
00:36:27,916 --> 00:36:31,285
An empty cage . And now - -

340
00:36:33,857 --> 00:36:37,120
You can do magic . Teach me .

341
00:36:37,120 --> 00:36:40,955
It is no magic . It is what we call optics .

342
00:36:40,955 --> 00:36:44,856
Separate pictures which become one in the spinning .

343
00:36:44,856 --> 00:36:47,950
It is truth , but truth is not always appearance .

344
00:36:55,462 --> 00:36:58,724
[ Inaudible Arguing ]

345
00:37:38,070 --> 00:37:40,797
What are you running from , Magistrate Philipse ?

346
00:37:40,797 --> 00:37:43,632
- Damn you , Crane . - You had a mind to help me ?

347
00:37:43,632 --> 00:37:47,296
- Yes , and it 's put me in mortal dread - - - Of what ?

348
00:37:47,296 --> 00:37:50,236
Of powers against which there is no defense . Come .

349
00:37:50,236 --> 00:37:52,272
How did you know the Widow Winship was expecting a child ?

350
00:37:52,272 --> 00:37:55,533
- She told me . - Then I deduce you are the father .

351
00:37:55,533 --> 00:37:57,038
I am not the father .

352
00:37:57,038 --> 00:37:59,232
Did she tell you the name of the child 's father ?

353
00:37:59,232 --> 00:38:02,331
Yes , she did . She came to me ...

354
00:38:02,331 --> 00:38:06,307
for advice as town magistrate to protect the rights of her child .

355
00:38:06,307 --> 00:38:09,239
I was bound by my oath of office to keep the secret , but - -

356
00:38:09,239 --> 00:38:12,867
- Do you believe the father killed her ? - The Horseman killed her .

357
00:38:12,867 --> 00:38:15,671
How often do I have to tell you there is no Horseman .

358
00:38:15,671 --> 00:38:18,335
Never was a Horseman , and never will be a Horseman .

359
00:38:18,335 --> 00:38:20,343
What is that thing ?

360
00:38:20,343 --> 00:38:23,003
My talisman . It protects me from the Horseman .

361
00:38:23,003 --> 00:38:26,341
You , a magistrate and your head full of such nonsense .

362
00:38:26,341 --> 00:38:29,038
- Tell me the name of ... .. - [ Sheep Bleating ]

363
00:38:29,038 --> 00:38:32,239
[ Bleating ]

364
00:38:32,239 --> 00:38:35,212
[ Thunderclaps ]

365
00:38:35,212 --> 00:38:38,213
- [ Thunderclaps ] - [ Squeaking ]

366
00:38:39,982 --> 00:38:42,470
[ Owl Hooting ]

367
00:38:44,416 --> 00:38:46,814
[ Horse Whinnying ]

368
00:38:48,217 --> 00:38:50,149
Oh , my God !

369
00:39:33,461 --> 00:39:35,394
[ Knocking ]

370
00:39:35,394 --> 00:39:38,622
Constable Crane ? Constable Crane ?

371
00:39:38,622 --> 00:39:42,151
Has he not come out at all ?

372
00:39:46,731 --> 00:39:49,629
- It was a Headless Horseman . - You must not excite yourself .

373
00:39:49,629 --> 00:39:52,722
- But it was a Headless Horseman . - Of course . That 's why you 're here .

374
00:39:52,722 --> 00:39:56,788
No , you must believe me . It was a Horseman , a dead one . Headless .

375
00:39:56,788 --> 00:40:00,129
- I know . - You don 't know . You were not there .

376
00:40:00,129 --> 00:40:03,689
- It 's all true . - Of course it is . Everyone told you .

377
00:40:05,335 --> 00:40:07,801
I ... saw him .

378
00:40:13,336 --> 00:40:15,894
I suppose it 's back to the city , then .

379
00:41:06,013 --> 00:41:10,241
[ Door Creaking ]

380
00:41:33,818 --> 00:41:35,751
[ Gasps ]

381
00:41:38,719 --> 00:41:42,413
All right , this time I will get to New York myself .

382
00:41:42,413 --> 00:41:44,918
I won 't be fobbed off with an amateur deductor .

383
00:41:57,056 --> 00:41:59,750
This time . it 's a magistrate that 's dead ... .

384
00:41:59,750 --> 00:42:04,313
Gentlemen . I need able men to go with me into the Western Woods .

385
00:42:04,313 --> 00:42:07,653
You ? We thought you 'd shot your bolt .

386
00:42:07,653 --> 00:42:09,418
I have faced my fears ,

387
00:42:09,418 --> 00:42:11,719
and come out determined to locate the Horseman 's grave .

388
00:42:11,719 --> 00:42:14,850
In short , to pit myself against a murdering ghost .

389
00:42:16,560 --> 00:42:18,924
Who 's with me ?

390
00:42:20,827 --> 00:42:21,577
Me .

391
00:42:24,770 --> 00:42:27,703
The Van Garretts . Widow Winship .

392
00:42:27,703 --> 00:42:29,828
Your father Jonathan Masbath .

393
00:42:29,828 --> 00:42:33,268
And now Philipse . Something must connect them .

394
00:42:33,268 --> 00:42:36,998
Did your father have dealings with the Van Garretts ?

395
00:42:36,998 --> 00:42:41,267
He worked for them . We lived in the coach house .

396
00:42:41,267 --> 00:42:43,465
It 's nothing .

397
00:42:43,465 --> 00:42:47,439
But there was something that happened one night a week before the murder .

398
00:42:47,439 --> 00:42:50,599
An argument upstairs between father and son .

399
00:42:50,599 --> 00:42:53,540
And my father was later sent for by Mr. Van Garrett .

400
00:42:55,609 --> 00:42:58,939
An argument between father and son .

401
00:42:58,939 --> 00:43:02,703
After which the elder Van Garrett sent for his servant Masbath .

402
00:43:02,703 --> 00:43:06,870
- Listen . - I hear nothing .

403
00:43:06,870 --> 00:43:09,468
Nor I. No birds .

404
00:43:09,468 --> 00:43:13,273
No crickets . It 's all gone so quiet .

405
00:43:21,414 --> 00:43:23,142
Quicken pace .

406
00:44:03,856 --> 00:44:06,981
[ Door Creaking ]

407
00:44:12,190 --> 00:44:14,281
Pardon our intrusion .

408
00:44:14,281 --> 00:44:18,723
- But perhaps you could help us . - You 're from the hollow .

409
00:44:18,723 --> 00:44:21,520
Yes , in a way .

410
00:44:24,060 --> 00:44:29,152
I should like to say , I make no assumptions about your occupation .

411
00:44:29,152 --> 00:44:31,785
Nor your ways , which , which - -

412
00:44:31,785 --> 00:44:35,624
Which are nothing to me , whatever you are .

413
00:44:35,624 --> 00:44:38,025
Each to his own .

414
00:44:41,296 --> 00:44:42,045
Oh .

415
00:44:47,930 --> 00:44:50,522
Do you know of the Horseman , ma 'am ?

416
00:44:50,522 --> 00:44:54,326
- The Hessian ? - [ Makes Slicing Sound ]

417
00:44:55,765 --> 00:44:58,027
That will be him , ma 'am .

418
00:44:58,027 --> 00:45:01,532
You , come with me .

419
00:45:01,532 --> 00:45:03,896
Go out child . Keep away .

420
00:45:03,896 --> 00:45:06,627
Whatever you hear . keep away .

421
00:45:13,136 --> 00:45:15,625
What might he hear that he must keep away from ?

422
00:45:21,470 --> 00:45:25,631
He rides ... to the hollow and back .

423
00:45:25,631 --> 00:45:28,830
I hear him , I smell the blood on him .

424
00:45:28,830 --> 00:45:32,702
Do you ? Well ,

425
00:45:32,702 --> 00:45:36,830
I am here to find him and make him stop .

426
00:45:36,830 --> 00:45:39,737
[ Bat Chirping ]

427
00:45:44,242 --> 00:45:46,674
You seek knowledge of the netherworld ? I can show you .

428
00:45:55,644 --> 00:45:59,667
- What are you doing ? - [ Sniffing ] Don 't move or speak .

429
00:45:59,667 --> 00:46:03,370
- When the other comes , I will hold him . - The other ?

430
00:46:03,370 --> 00:46:05,843
Silence . [ Sniffing ] He comes now .

431
00:46:14,380 --> 00:46:16,313
Madam ?

432
00:46:18,948 --> 00:46:21,380
Madam , do you hear me ?

433
00:46:29,683 --> 00:46:33,309
[ Growling ]

434
00:46:33,309 --> 00:46:37,317
You seek the warrior bathed in blood . The Headless Horseman .

435
00:46:37,317 --> 00:46:40,476
Follow the Indian trail to where the sun dies .

436
00:46:40,476 --> 00:46:43,178
Follow it to the Tree of the Dead .

437
00:46:43,178 --> 00:46:47,016
Climb down to the Horseman 's resting place .

438
00:46:53,655 --> 00:46:56,178
- We 're leaving . - What happened ?

439
00:46:56,178 --> 00:46:59,110
We 're leaving now .

440
00:47:00,444 --> 00:47:02,240
We take the Indian trail to the Tree of the Dead .

441
00:47:02,240 --> 00:47:05,767
- How will we recognize it ? - Without difficulty , I rather fear .

442
00:47:05,767 --> 00:47:08,176
Then climb down to the Horseman 's resting place .

443
00:47:08,176 --> 00:47:11,111
- His camp ? - His grave .

444
00:47:20,782 --> 00:47:23,180
Stay here .

445
00:47:59,122 --> 00:48:01,816
Halt and turn . I have a pistol aimed .

446
00:48:04,090 --> 00:48:06,488
Katrina .

447
00:48:06,488 --> 00:48:08,887
I might have killed you . Why have you come ?

448
00:48:08,887 --> 00:48:12,186
Because no one else would go with you .

449
00:48:12,186 --> 00:48:14,884
I am now twice the man .

450
00:48:15,859 --> 00:48:19,383
It is your white magic .

451
00:48:20,527 --> 00:48:22,891
Pardon my intrusion .

452
00:48:22,891 --> 00:48:26,291
I think you 'd better come and look at this .

453
00:49:08,503 --> 00:49:10,594
The Tree of the Dead .

454
00:49:26,839 --> 00:49:28,465
Blood .

455
00:49:31,406 --> 00:49:34,339
Stay where you are .

456
00:50:13,882 --> 00:50:18,406
- What is it ? - Just stay where you are . Don 't move .

457
00:50:32,919 --> 00:50:35,749
This tree is a gateway .

458
00:50:35,749 --> 00:50:39,343
A gateway between two worlds .

459
00:50:51,155 --> 00:50:55,020
This ground has been disturbed . The soil is loose .

460
00:50:55,020 --> 00:50:56,953
Bring the shovel .

461
00:51:15,527 --> 00:51:19,790
The skull is gone . Taken .

462
00:51:19,790 --> 00:51:22,952
That is why the Horseman returns from the grave .

463
00:51:22,952 --> 00:51:26,859
To take heads till his own is restored to him .

464
00:51:26,859 --> 00:51:28,986
[ Thunderclaps ]

465
00:51:44,666 --> 00:51:47,098
Ichabod ?

466
00:51:52,433 --> 00:51:54,956
[ Whinnies ]

467
00:51:57,368 --> 00:51:59,335
[ Whinnying ]

468
00:52:17,039 --> 00:52:18,664
Hyah ! Hyah !

469
00:52:31,408 --> 00:52:34,081
- [ Thunderclaps ] - [ Horse Whinnies ]

470
00:52:35,048 --> 00:52:38,606
Split up . Glenn . Theodore .

471
00:52:57,653 --> 00:53:01,108
Don 't pick your teeth . You will teach Thomas bad habits .

472
00:53:01,108 --> 00:53:04,176
I am a bad habit . There 's nothing for it .

473
00:53:04,176 --> 00:53:06,277
Oh , isn 't there ?

474
00:53:07,987 --> 00:53:10,284
[ Chuckles ]

475
00:53:21,424 --> 00:53:25,016
[ Wind Howling ]

476
00:53:25,016 --> 00:53:28,421
- Come on , let 's get ready for bed . - Yes .

477
00:53:34,660 --> 00:53:36,785
[ Thunderclaps ]

478
00:53:49,596 --> 00:53:52,756
Beth , run .

479
00:54:12,667 --> 00:54:14,600
Stay quiet .

480
00:54:26,203 --> 00:54:28,795
- [ Panting , Gasps ] - [ Door Opens ]

481
00:54:56,842 --> 00:54:59,775
- [ Beth Gasps ] - [ Sword Slashes ]

482
00:55:25,547 --> 00:55:28,070
[ Thunderclaps ]

483
00:55:44,618 --> 00:55:46,846
[ Thomas Screams ]

484
00:55:46,846 --> 00:55:49,817
[ Screaming ]

485
00:56:13,357 --> 00:56:15,687
[ Whinnying ]

486
00:56:58,765 --> 00:57:03,460
- Wait ! He 's not after you . - I will get him .

487
00:57:22,704 --> 00:57:24,1000
We cannot win this .

488
00:57:34,038 --> 00:57:34,838
[ Loud Footsteps ]

489
00:57:38,973 --> 00:57:41,304
[ Footsteps Continue ]

490
00:57:47,308 --> 00:57:48,307
Aah !

491
00:58:18,847 --> 00:58:21,746
[ Thunderclaps ]

492
00:58:23,815 --> 00:58:27,475
Remarkable . A wound like this should have killed him . But it needs no stitch ,

493
00:58:27,475 --> 00:58:30,175
... . and there 's hardly a loss of blood . - [ Gasps ]

494
00:58:30,175 --> 00:58:32,580
You must be still .

495
00:58:32,580 --> 00:58:37,982
- The fever is on you . - Katrina .

496
00:58:37,982 --> 00:58:42,507
Nostradamus , Mediamus , Milk of Mercy ,

497
00:58:42,507 --> 00:58:45,575
in media noslaudamas .

498
00:59:01,729 --> 00:59:05,423
Katrina , I tried to stop Brom , but - -

499
00:59:05,423 --> 00:59:08,929
Shh . Drink this down . It will make you sleep .

500
00:59:08,929 --> 00:59:14,692
The Horseman was not set to kill Brom or me . Had Brom not attacked him ... .

501
00:59:14,692 --> 00:59:16,957
Later . Rest now .

502
00:59:16,957 --> 00:59:20,486
I have discovered something . The Horseman does not kill at random .

503
00:59:20,486 --> 00:59:23,964
His victims are chosen by someone who controls him .

504
00:59:23,964 --> 00:59:26,465
By that very person who took his skull .

505
00:59:26,465 --> 00:59:29,364
Someone who knew where to dig .

506
00:59:29,364 --> 00:59:32,526
Someone of flesh and blood , as I have always said .

507
00:59:32,526 --> 00:59:35,863
- These are ravings . - Shh . Drink .

508
01:00:25,044 --> 01:00:27,533
[ Lady Crane 's Voice ] Ichabod .

509
01:00:41,381 --> 01:00:42,460
[ Gasps ]

510
01:00:46,048 --> 01:00:48,844
Shh . You were dreaming .

511
01:00:48,844 --> 01:00:53,611
Yes . Things I had forgotten .

512
01:00:56,551 --> 01:01:00,541
- And would not like to remember . - Tell me what you dreamt .

513
01:01:00,541 --> 01:01:03,709
My mother was an innocent .

514
01:01:03,709 --> 01:01:07,081
A child of nature .

515
01:01:07,081 --> 01:01:09,846
Condemned .

516
01:01:09,846 --> 01:01:12,785
Murdered ... by my father .

517
01:01:12,785 --> 01:01:14,945
Murdered by ... .

518
01:01:14,945 --> 01:01:17,385
Murdered to save her soul ...

519
01:01:17,385 --> 01:01:22,855
by a Bible-black tyrant behind a mask of righteousness .

520
01:01:22,855 --> 01:01:26,117
I was seven ... when I lost my faith .

521
01:01:28,657 --> 01:01:30,850
What do you believe in ?

522
01:01:30,850 --> 01:01:34,948
Sense and reason . Cause and consequence .

523
01:01:36,392 --> 01:01:39,256
I should not have come to this place ...

524
01:01:39,256 --> 01:01:42,656
where my rational mind has been so controverted by the spirit world .

525
01:01:42,656 --> 01:01:48,182
Will you take nothing from Sleepy Hollow that was worth the coming here ?

526
01:01:48,182 --> 01:01:48,932
No .

527
01:01:50,260 --> 01:01:52,284
No , not nothing .

528
01:01:54,862 --> 01:01:57,556
A kiss from a lovely young woman ...

529
01:01:57,556 --> 01:02:00,356
before she saw my face or knew my name .

530
01:02:00,356 --> 01:02:04,328
Yes , without sense or reason .

531
01:02:08,631 --> 01:02:11,257
Forgive me , I speak of kisses ...

532
01:02:11,257 --> 01:02:14,355
and you have lost your brave man , Brom .

533
01:02:16,365 --> 01:02:19,332
I have shed my tears for Brom .

534
01:02:19,332 --> 01:02:22,491
And yet my heart is not broken .

535
01:02:23,568 --> 01:02:25,898
Do you think me wicked ?

536
01:02:25,898 --> 01:02:26,647
No .

537
01:02:28,768 --> 01:02:31,394
Perhaps there is a bit of a witch in you , Katrina .

538
01:02:31,394 --> 01:02:33,561
Why do you say that ?

539
01:02:33,561 --> 01:02:36,500
Because you have bewitched me .

540
01:02:48,705 --> 01:02:49,455
Oh .

541
01:02:50,706 --> 01:02:55,332
- You slept like the dead . - You 're too kind to me .

542
01:02:55,332 --> 01:02:58,306
I do not look to be served by the lady of the house .

543
01:02:58,306 --> 01:03:02,670
Nor would you be , but that the servant girl has vanished .

544
01:03:02,670 --> 01:03:07,333
- Sarah ? - Run away like so many others .

545
01:03:07,333 --> 01:03:10,205
They 're all leaving in fear .

546
01:03:10,205 --> 01:03:13,208
Where is Katrina ?

547
01:03:13,208 --> 01:03:17,300
She watched over you till dawn . Now it is her turn to sleep .

548
01:03:24,146 --> 01:03:27,340
Well , I am fit for another day , I think .

549
01:03:27,340 --> 01:03:31,417
Fit enough to face a mortal adversary .

550
01:03:33,551 --> 01:03:35,381
Dr. Lancaster .

551
01:03:35,381 --> 01:03:37,475
Reverend Steenwyck .

552
01:03:37,475 --> 01:03:38,474
Hmm .

553
01:03:39,552 --> 01:03:45,282
Notary Hardenbrook . And Magistrate Philipse .

554
01:03:46,753 --> 01:03:49,720
Who tried to cut and run and lost his head .

555
01:03:49,720 --> 01:03:52,550
All frightened men , arguing together

556
01:03:52,550 --> 01:03:56,214
on the very night Magistrate Philipse was killed .

557
01:03:57,789 --> 01:04:00,312
There is conspiracy here .

558
01:04:04,357 --> 01:04:09,154
The doctor . The reverend . the notary and the magistrate .

559
01:04:11,858 --> 01:04:15,450
What is this secret that unites them ?

560
01:04:16,859 --> 01:04:19,052
Magistrate Philipse knew ...

561
01:04:19,052 --> 01:04:22,150
there were five bodies to four graves .

562
01:04:22,150 --> 01:04:24,853
He knew the widow was pregnant .

563
01:04:24,853 --> 01:04:29,122
He could not tell me the name of the father .

564
01:04:29,122 --> 01:04:32,821
What does this point to ?

565
01:04:37,963 --> 01:04:41,919
We must proceed by a process of elimination .

566
01:04:41,919 --> 01:04:44,828
I shall make a list of every man and woman in Sleepy Hollow ...

567
01:04:44,828 --> 01:04:48,388
starting with its chief citizen . Baltus Van Tassel .

568
01:04:50,933 --> 01:04:53,297
I feel we 're getting very close .

569
01:04:53,297 --> 01:04:58,857
I suppose Baltus is the chief citizen now that old Van Garrett is dead .

570
01:04:58,857 --> 01:05:02,924
Yes , the Van Garretts .

571
01:05:02,924 --> 01:05:05,560
I 'd almost forgotten them .

572
01:05:14,937 --> 01:05:17,335
Come with me .

573
01:05:17,335 --> 01:05:20,962
- Where ? - To Notary Hardenbrook 's .

574
01:05:20,962 --> 01:05:23,164
- Have you thought of something ? - Yes .

575
01:05:23,164 --> 01:05:24,003
I have .

576
01:05:40,675 --> 01:05:43,039
Hopeless .

577
01:05:50,777 --> 01:05:54,972
My father 's satchel . Why is it here ?

578
01:05:57,212 --> 01:05:59,542
[ Gasps ]

579
01:05:59,542 --> 01:06:02,044
- Leave me alone . - Notary Hardenbrook .

580
01:06:02,044 --> 01:06:04,477
Leave me alone .

581
01:06:04,477 --> 01:06:07,480
As soon as you show me the last will and testament of old man Van Garrett .

582
01:06:07,480 --> 01:06:10,537
The will leaves everything to his son .

583
01:06:10,537 --> 01:06:14,877
Who died with him . So the estate passes to the next of kin .

584
01:06:14,877 --> 01:06:17,847
Naturally . All legal and above board .

585
01:06:17,847 --> 01:06:19,096
Sir ?

586
01:06:21,483 --> 01:06:24,314
I am a dead man . No , no .

587
01:06:25,918 --> 01:06:28,680
Van Garrett 's seal ... broken .

588
01:06:31,318 --> 01:06:34,251
Seems Van Garrett made a new will just before he died .

589
01:06:34,251 --> 01:06:36,683
Naming ...

590
01:06:36,683 --> 01:06:38,844
Widow Winship ?

591
01:06:38,844 --> 01:06:40,819
And here , look .

592
01:06:40,819 --> 01:06:44,547
- A marriage certificate . - Aha !

593
01:06:44,547 --> 01:06:47,213
Old Van Garrett secretly married the widow .

594
01:06:47,213 --> 01:06:50,813
Left everything to her and her unborn child .

595
01:06:50,813 --> 01:06:54,754
So the new will stood between the Van Garrett fortune

596
01:06:54,754 --> 01:06:57,017
and the person who would have otherwise inherited everything .

597
01:06:57,017 --> 01:07:02,352
It 's true . But we four were drawn in against our will !

598
01:07:02,352 --> 01:07:04,982
- Your will ? - He means ... .

599
01:07:04,982 --> 01:07:09,515
Of course . The four town elders .

600
01:07:09,515 --> 01:07:12,252
Now I see what parts you had to play .

601
01:07:13,927 --> 01:07:17,382
Reverend Steenwyck knew the secret because he performed the marriage .

602
01:07:17,382 --> 01:07:20,359
Dr. Lancaster attended the pregnant woman .

603
01:07:20,359 --> 01:07:23,588
Magistrate Philipse gave protection of the law .

604
01:07:23,588 --> 01:07:26,823
And Notary Hardenbrook concealed the documents ...

605
01:07:26,823 --> 01:07:30,056
which had been entrusted by Van Garrett to his faithful servant .

606
01:07:30,056 --> 01:07:32,528
The four conspirators drawn into the plot .

607
01:07:32,528 --> 01:07:36,496
We did not know it was a murdering plot .

608
01:07:36,496 --> 01:07:38,724
But I have not finished , sir .

609
01:07:38,724 --> 01:07:41,958
First , the Van Garretts , father and son , slain by a horseman ...

610
01:07:41,958 --> 01:07:44,226
raised from the grave to chop heads .

611
01:07:44,226 --> 01:07:48,323
Now , up pops a widow with a claim on the fortune . Off with her head .

612
01:07:48,323 --> 01:07:51,561
But murder begets murder .

613
01:07:51,561 --> 01:07:55,465
It was the servant , Jonathan Masbath .

614
01:07:55,465 --> 01:07:57,865
The night father and son quarrelled over the new will ,

615
01:07:57,865 --> 01:08:02,528
Jonathan Masbath was summoned upstairs to bear witness .

616
01:08:02,528 --> 01:08:07,195
Here is his signature . I am afraid it was his death warrant , young Masbath .

617
01:08:07,195 --> 01:08:10,260
The Horseman came for him .

618
01:08:10,260 --> 01:08:14,964
Came for him at the bidding of someone who had power over him .

619
01:08:14,964 --> 01:08:18,437
Someone who dug in the earth in the Western Woods and stole the skull .

620
01:08:18,437 --> 01:08:20,972
The missing head which must be restored to the Horseman ...

621
01:08:20,972 --> 01:08:22,972
before he will return to hell .

622
01:08:22,972 --> 01:08:25,233
Someone who stood to gain or lose a fortune .

623
01:08:25,233 --> 01:08:29,400
None other than Van Garrett 's next of kin .

624
01:08:29,400 --> 01:08:31,770
Baltus Van Tassel .

625
01:08:37,076 --> 01:08:40,270
Katrina ? Why are you in my room ?

626
01:08:40,270 --> 01:08:43,708
Because it is yours .

627
01:08:44,845 --> 01:08:47,277
Was it wicked of me ?

628
01:08:47,277 --> 01:08:50,368
No , no , not at all .

629
01:08:52,213 --> 01:08:54,372
I missed you . Where did you go ?

630
01:08:54,372 --> 01:08:57,345
To the Notary . I had questions to ask Hardenbrook .

631
01:08:57,345 --> 01:08:59,380
Did you learn anything of interest ?

632
01:09:01,747 --> 01:09:03,407
Perhaps .

633
01:09:03,407 --> 01:09:06,447
- My father ... . - Your father ?

634
01:09:06,447 --> 01:09:10,380
Yes . My father thinks you should return to New York .

635
01:09:10,380 --> 01:09:13,779
Really ? Why is that ?

636
01:09:13,779 --> 01:09:16,942
I don 't know .

637
01:09:16,942 --> 01:09:20,211
Perhaps he looked in your ledger and did not like what he saw .

638
01:09:25,118 --> 01:09:29,676
- What have you there ? - Evidence . I am sorry , I must ask you ...

639
01:09:29,676 --> 01:09:31,912
Then I will leave you to your thoughts .

640
01:09:41,255 --> 01:09:43,221
[ Gasps ]

641
01:09:46,022 --> 01:09:48,853
- It 's just a spider . - Kill it . Kill it .

642
01:09:48,853 --> 01:09:51,014
No. no. stomp it !

643
01:09:53,157 --> 01:09:55,386
- There 's something under here . - What is it ?

644
01:09:57,758 --> 01:10:01,623
- Help me move the bed . - No , I mustn 't . You do it .

645
01:10:07,026 --> 01:10:11,551
The evil eye . It is someone casting spells against you .

646
01:10:13,394 --> 01:10:15,360
The evil eye ?

647
01:10:21,995 --> 01:10:24,553
[ Thumping Sound ]

648
01:11:06,771 --> 01:11:08,703
Wait here .

649
01:12:23,753 --> 01:12:28,846
Katrina , you took the evidence and burned it .

650
01:12:28,846 --> 01:12:31,409
So you would not have it to accuse my father .

651
01:12:31,409 --> 01:12:34,511
I accuse no one . But if there is guilt ,

652
01:12:34,511 --> 01:12:37,180
I cannot alter it no matter how much it grieves me .

653
01:12:37,180 --> 01:12:39,585
And no spells of yours can alter it , either .

654
01:12:39,585 --> 01:12:43,782
Your father has the motive . It is he who stands to profit from these murders .

655
01:12:43,782 --> 01:12:46,789
If you knew him , you would not have such harsh thoughts about him .

656
01:12:46,789 --> 01:12:49,619
Nor if you felt anything for me .

657
01:12:49,619 --> 01:12:51,623
I am pinioned by a chain of reasoning .

658
01:12:51,623 --> 01:12:53,919
Why else did his friends conspire to conceal ...

659
01:12:53,919 --> 01:12:58,254
You are the constable . So find another chain of reasoning and let me be .

660
01:12:58,254 --> 01:13:03,225
I cannot . Nor the one or the other . And I am heartsick with it .

661
01:13:03,225 --> 01:13:08,275
I think you have no heart . And I had a mind once to give you mine .

662
01:13:09,528 --> 01:13:12,872
Yes , I think you loved me that day

663
01:13:12,872 --> 01:13:16,252
when you followed me into the Western Woods to have braved such peril .

664
01:13:16,252 --> 01:13:19,261
What peril was there for me if it was my own father

665
01:13:19,261 --> 01:13:21,261
who controlled the Headless Horseman ?

666
01:13:25,998 --> 01:13:29,930
Good-bye , Ichabod Crane . I curse the day you came to Sleepy Hollow .

667
01:13:29,930 --> 01:13:32,362
[ Whinnies ]

668
01:13:35,767 --> 01:13:40,393
- She will not see you . - Did she say anything ?

669
01:13:40,393 --> 01:13:44,161
[ Sighs ] Only that she will not come down .

670
01:13:45,602 --> 01:13:47,864
I see . Thank you .

671
01:13:47,864 --> 01:13:51,095
Constable ?

672
01:13:51,095 --> 01:13:55,569
You have not asked me how I have hurt my hand since yesterday ,

673
01:13:55,569 --> 01:13:58,103
which would have been polite .

674
01:13:59,405 --> 01:14:01,871
In fact , you have been as careful ...

675
01:14:01,871 --> 01:14:05,768
not to look at it as not to mention it .

676
01:14:07,105 --> 01:14:10,163
Yes . I am sorry . How did you ... .

677
01:14:10,163 --> 01:14:14,105
- I know you saw me . - What ?

678
01:14:14,105 --> 01:14:17,334
I know you followed last night ,

679
01:14:17,334 --> 01:14:20,568
and you must promise not to tell my husband what you saw .

680
01:14:20,568 --> 01:14:22,574
Promise me .

681
01:14:23,609 --> 01:14:25,472
The town is in ferment .

682
01:14:25,472 --> 01:14:28,134
Horror piled on tragedy . Hardenbrook is dead .

683
01:14:28,134 --> 01:14:32,404
- Oh , no . That harmless old man ? - Hanged himself in the night .

684
01:14:32,404 --> 01:14:33,773
Hanged himself ?

685
01:14:33,773 --> 01:14:35,742
Reverend Steenwyck 's called a meeting in the church tonight .

686
01:14:35,742 --> 01:14:39,369
Every man , woman and child is going to speak out against you .

687
01:14:39,369 --> 01:14:42,412
If you are wise . you will leave this place .

688
01:14:43,613 --> 01:14:45,545
What is that ?

689
01:14:45,545 --> 01:14:47,909
I was careless with the kitchen knife .

690
01:14:47,909 --> 01:14:50,310
[ Baltus ] The wound looks angry .

691
01:14:50,310 --> 01:14:53,972
I will bind it later with wild-arrow root flowers .

692
01:14:53,972 --> 01:14:56,017
I know where some grow .

693
01:14:56,851 --> 01:14:59,841
[ Church Bell Ringing ]

694
01:14:59,841 --> 01:15:02,350
[ Humming ]

695
01:15:04,953 --> 01:15:07,249
Come on , hurry up .

696
01:15:07,249 --> 01:15:09,718
The meeting bell started to ring .

697
01:15:11,286 --> 01:15:14,879
[ Thunderclaps ]

698
01:15:19,055 --> 01:15:21,886
[ Thunderclaps ]

699
01:15:24,690 --> 01:15:27,349
[ Bell Ringing ]

700
01:15:32,791 --> 01:15:34,280
The Horseman .

701
01:15:36,358 --> 01:15:39,950
- Katrina . The Horseman saved me . - Father ?

702
01:15:42,026 --> 01:15:45,618
He killed her . The Horseman killed your stepmother .

703
01:15:45,618 --> 01:15:49,922
- [ Thunderclaps ] - [ Horse Whinnying ]

704
01:15:54,429 --> 01:15:56,019
Oh , God !

705
01:16:07,498 --> 01:16:09,362
[ Man ] Fire !

706
01:16:09,362 --> 01:16:11,364
[ Whinnying ]

707
01:16:11,364 --> 01:16:14,024
[ Shouting , Screaming ]

708
01:16:26,135 --> 01:16:29,431
You will kill us all . You 're the one the Horseman wants .

709
01:16:50,506 --> 01:16:52,870
He cannot enter .

710
01:17:01,142 --> 01:17:04,802
- The Horseman cannot enter . - Why should we die for you ?

711
01:17:04,802 --> 01:17:06,967
The Horseman cannot enter . He cannot cross the gate .

712
01:17:06,967 --> 01:17:09,133
We have to save ourselves .

713
01:17:10,777 --> 01:17:13,767
The next person that lays a hand on me will get a bullet .

714
01:17:15,644 --> 01:17:18,440
He 's coming back .

715
01:17:21,179 --> 01:17:22,701
[ Whinnies ]

716
01:17:24,713 --> 01:17:28,043
Enough have died already . It 's time to confess our sins .

717
01:17:28,043 --> 01:17:31,080
- What is it that you know ? - Your four friends played you false .

718
01:17:31,080 --> 01:17:33,239
We were devilishly possessed by one who ... .

719
01:17:34,448 --> 01:17:37,040
- [ Gunshot ] - [ Gasps ]

720
01:17:42,282 --> 01:17:45,977
Get out of my way ! Stand back ! Stay back !

721
01:17:56,719 --> 01:17:59,879
Back ! Stand back .

722
01:18:03,020 --> 01:18:07,316
There is a conspiracy here , and I will shake it out .

723
01:18:11,988 --> 01:18:13,750
[ Screams ]

724
01:19:23,931 --> 01:19:26,955
It was an evil spirit possessed you .

725
01:19:26,955 --> 01:19:29,464
I pray God it is satisfied now , and that you find peace .

726
01:19:29,464 --> 01:19:32,657
The evil eye 's done its work .

727
01:19:32,657 --> 01:19:37,133
My life is over , spared for a lifetime of horrors in my sleep ,

728
01:19:37,133 --> 01:19:40,759
waking each day to grief .

729
01:19:46,602 --> 01:19:48,568
Good-bye , Katrina .

730
01:20:18,975 --> 01:20:22,066
[ Hoof beats ]

731
01:20:22,066 --> 01:20:23,315
Whoa .

732
01:20:24,843 --> 01:20:28,367
You think it was Katrina , don 't you ?

733
01:20:28,367 --> 01:20:30,637
That can never be uttered .

734
01:20:30,637 --> 01:20:34,075
A strange sort of witch , with a kind and loving heart .

735
01:20:34,075 --> 01:20:36,577
- How can you think so ? - I have good reason .

736
01:20:36,577 --> 01:20:39,544
- Then you are bewitched by reason . - I am beaten down by it .

737
01:20:45,481 --> 01:20:49,413
It is a hard lesson for a hard world , and you had better learn it .

738
01:20:49,413 --> 01:20:54,244
Villainy wears many masks . None so dangerous as the mask of virtue .

739
01:21:01,683 --> 01:21:03,616
Farewell .

740
01:22:33,868 --> 01:22:37,301
- Return the coach . Turn around now . - What ?

741
01:22:45,636 --> 01:22:47,830
Whoa .

742
01:22:47,830 --> 01:22:50,063
[ Knocking ]

743
01:22:50,063 --> 01:22:52,070
Pardon my intrusion .

744
01:23:02,807 --> 01:23:06,830
No blood flow , no clotting , no healing .

745
01:23:09,541 --> 01:23:13,474
When this cut was made , this woman was already dead .

746
01:23:23,377 --> 01:23:25,309
Dear stepdaughter .

747
01:23:27,545 --> 01:23:29,738
You look as if you 'd seen a ghost .

748
01:23:37,746 --> 01:23:39,337
Yah !

749
01:24:01,184 --> 01:24:05,675
Rise up once more , my Dark Avenger .

750
01:24:05,675 --> 01:24:07,911
One more night of beheading .

751
01:24:07,911 --> 01:24:10,578
Rise up with your sword .

752
01:24:10,578 --> 01:24:14,779
A head ... for a head .

753
01:24:14,779 --> 01:24:17,911
My unholy Horseman , rise .

754
01:24:17,911 --> 01:24:22,921
[ Lady Van Tassel ] Come now for ... Katrina .

755
01:24:24,922 --> 01:24:26,786
[ Whinnying ]

756
01:24:35,692 --> 01:24:37,624
Awake at last .

757
01:24:37,624 --> 01:24:41,352
Did you think it was all a nasty dream ?

758
01:24:41,352 --> 01:24:43,483
Father saw the Horseman kill you .

759
01:24:43,483 --> 01:24:47,959
He saw the Horseman come towards me with his sword unsheathed ,

760
01:24:47,959 --> 01:24:52,221
but it is I who govern the Horseman , my dear .

761
01:24:52,221 --> 01:24:54,760
and Baltus did not stay to watch .

762
01:24:54,760 --> 01:24:56,761
Yah ! Yah !

763
01:24:59,029 --> 01:25:02,757
- But there was a body . - The servant girl , Sarah .

764
01:25:02,757 --> 01:25:05,591
[ Lady Van Tassel 's Voice ] And I always thought she was useless .

765
01:25:08,764 --> 01:25:11,595
But it seems she had a purpose after all .

766
01:25:16,199 --> 01:25:18,256
Who are you ?

767
01:25:18,256 --> 01:25:22,357
My family name was Archer .

768
01:25:22,357 --> 01:25:24,025
The Archer .

769
01:25:25,567 --> 01:25:27,761
[ Whinnying ]

770
01:25:30,601 --> 01:25:35,035
I lived with my father and mother and sister in a cottage not far from here .

771
01:25:35,035 --> 01:25:37,898
Until one day my father died . The landlord ,

772
01:25:37,898 --> 01:25:42,370
who had received many years of loyal service from my parents , evicted us .

773
01:25:42,370 --> 01:25:44,700
No one in this God-fearing town ...

774
01:25:44,700 --> 01:25:48,431
would take us in because my mother was suspected of witchcraft .

775
01:25:48,431 --> 01:25:51,437
But she schooled her daughters well ...

776
01:25:51,437 --> 01:25:54,097
while we lived as outcasts in the Western Woods .

777
01:25:55,340 --> 01:25:57,806
She died within a year .

778
01:26:02,375 --> 01:26:04,848
My sister and I remained in our refuge ,

779
01:26:04,848 --> 01:26:08,312
seeing not a soul .

780
01:26:08,312 --> 01:26:13,145
Until one day , whilst gathering firewood ,

781
01:26:13,145 --> 01:26:16,377
we crossed the path of the Hessian .

782
01:26:16,377 --> 01:26:18,575
- Shh . - [ Twig Snaps ]

783
01:26:20,218 --> 01:26:22,946
I saw his death .

784
01:26:22,946 --> 01:26:26,644
At that moment , I offered my soul to Satan ...

785
01:26:26,644 --> 01:26:32,380
if he would raise the Hessian from the grave to avenge me .

786
01:26:35,688 --> 01:26:38,984
- Avenge you ? - Against Van Garrett .

787
01:26:38,984 --> 01:26:42,647
The landlord who showed us no mercy and left us to starve , whilst ...

788
01:26:42,647 --> 01:26:47,451
Baltus Van Tassel and his simpering wife and girl child stole our home .

789
01:26:47,451 --> 01:26:51,115
I swore I would make myself mistress of all he had .

790
01:26:51,115 --> 01:26:53,816
The easiest part was the first .

791
01:26:53,816 --> 01:26:56,380
To enter your house as your mother 's sicknurse .

792
01:26:56,380 --> 01:27:00,050
and put her body into the grave and my own into the marriage bed .

793
01:27:00,050 --> 01:27:04,683
Not quite so easy was to secure my legacy .

794
01:27:04,683 --> 01:27:07,419
The widow had to go , of course ,

795
01:27:07,419 --> 01:27:09,721
and the servant Masbath .

796
01:27:09,721 --> 01:27:13,557
And just the other day , that silly midwife , Killian ,

797
01:27:13,557 --> 01:27:17,823
told me the widow had told her a big secret .

798
01:27:17,823 --> 01:27:20,294
And she told me this right in front of her husband .

799
01:27:20,294 --> 01:27:22,261
What a goose .

800
01:27:22,261 --> 01:27:25,126
So. another little job for the Horseman .

801
01:27:27,698 --> 01:27:33,097
But lust delivered the Reverend Steenwyck into my power .

802
01:27:34,832 --> 01:27:37,764
Fear did the same for the Notary Hardenbrook ...

803
01:27:37,764 --> 01:27:40,095
and the drunkard Philipse .

804
01:27:40,095 --> 01:27:42,690
And the doctor 's silence I exchanged ...

805
01:27:42,690 --> 01:27:48,257
for my complicity in his fornications with the servant girl . Sarah .

806
01:27:48,257 --> 01:27:50,631
Yes , you have everything now .

807
01:27:50,631 --> 01:27:55,397
No . You have , my dear , by your father 's will .

808
01:27:56,703 --> 01:27:59,670
I get everything in the event of your death .

809
01:28:01,071 --> 01:28:03,094
Oh. my sister. by the way .

810
01:28:03,094 --> 01:28:06,569
sadly passed away ...

811
01:28:08,372 --> 01:28:12,271
quite recently .

812
01:28:12,271 --> 01:28:14,465
[ Katrina ] You killed your own sister ?

813
01:28:14,465 --> 01:28:18,564
She brought it on herself by helping you and your master .

814
01:28:20,207 --> 01:28:23,470
[ Laughing ] You 're just in time to have your head cut off .

815
01:28:23,470 --> 01:28:28,271
The Horseman comes , and tonight he comes for you .

816
01:28:35,110 --> 01:28:37,077
Katrina .

817
01:28:42,245 --> 01:28:44,337
- Thank God . - [ Horse Whinnying ]

818
01:28:52,847 --> 01:28:55,040
Watch your head .

819
01:29:10,017 --> 01:29:13,381
To the roof ! I have an idea .

820
01:30:12,329 --> 01:30:14,795
Jump for the sails .

821
01:30:29,165 --> 01:30:30,631
[ Crane ] Jump .

822
01:30:35,433 --> 01:30:36,152
Hurry .

823
01:30:56,671 --> 01:31:00,434
- Is he dead ? - That 's the problem .

824
01:31:00,434 --> 01:31:02,664
He was dead to begin with .

825
01:31:08,906 --> 01:31:10,155
Hyah .

826
01:31:12,207 --> 01:31:14,696
[ Horse Whinnies ]

827
01:31:24,909 --> 01:31:26,352
- Where are we going ? - Anywhere but here .

828
01:31:26,352 --> 01:31:27,443
- Where are we going ? - Anywhere but here .

829
01:31:40,322 --> 01:31:42,220
Here . Take the reins .

830
01:31:52,224 --> 01:31:54,156
[ Gunshot ]

831
01:32:02,660 --> 01:32:04,592
Ichabod .

832
01:32:14,495 --> 01:32:15,494
Yah !

833
01:32:59,337 --> 01:33:00,176
My bag .

834
01:33:17,907 --> 01:33:19,998
Jump .

835
01:34:17,185 --> 01:34:20,310
[ Whinnying ]

836
01:34:22,386 --> 01:34:24,181
Still alive ?

837
01:34:24,181 --> 01:34:26,117
Run , Katrina .

838
01:34:26,117 --> 01:34:30,620
Yes , do run , and jump , and skip .

839
01:34:33,055 --> 01:34:36,510
- No ! - [ Gasps ]

840
01:34:39,223 --> 01:34:41,246
[ Thunderclaps ]

841
01:34:42,324 --> 01:34:45,757
Here . Take her .

842
01:34:45,757 --> 01:34:48,086
She 's yours .

843
01:34:51,492 --> 01:34:55,016
Sir , you 're not dead .

844
01:35:19,897 --> 01:35:21,693
[ Screams ]

845
01:35:35,000 --> 01:35:36,523
Horseman .

846
01:36:45,514 --> 01:36:47,310
[ Whinnies ]

847
01:36:57,283 --> 01:36:59,272
Hyah !

848
01:37:11,886 --> 01:37:13,135
Hyah !

849
01:37:41,458 --> 01:37:43,822
[ Gasps ]

850
01:38:06,862 --> 01:38:08,852
[ Whinnies ]

851
01:39:07,841 --> 01:39:12,501
Ahh . Just in time for a new century .

852
01:39:24,844 --> 01:39:27,004
You will soon get your bearings , young Masbath .

853
01:39:27,004 --> 01:39:29,510
The Bronx is up , the Battery 's down .

854
01:39:29,510 --> 01:39:32,636
And home is this way .

